diff --git a/game/assets/audio/vehicles/NOTICE.txt b/game/assets/audio/vehicles/NOTICE.txt
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/game/assets/audio/vehicles/NOTICE.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+Beat my track vehicle audio bank v1 — 2026-10-06
+
+Recorded engine, rolling and body source masters:
+Nox Sound Design, Essentials Series, CC0 1.0.
+https://nox-sound-design.itch.io/essentials-series-sfx-nox-sound
+
+Additional recorded engine source masters:
+Joseph SARDIN, “AC Cobra Engine”, BigSoundBank, CC0 1.0.
+https://bigsoundbank.com/ac-cobra-engine-s0534.html
+DenisChardonnet, “Motor car #1”, BigSoundBank, CC0 1.0.
+https://bigsoundbank.com/motor-car-1-s0290.html
+DenisChardonnet, “Motorcycle”, BigSoundBank, CC0 1.0.
+https://bigsoundbank.com/motorcycle-s0281.html
+
+Recorded tire squeal:
+“Car tire squeal skid loop” by audible-edge (Tom Haigh), edited into a loop
+by qubodup, licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported.
+https://opengameart.org/content/car-tire-squeal-skid-loop
+https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
+Changes: mono 44.1 kHz resampling, filtering, loop crossfade, loudness mastering
+and 16-bit dither. Attribution applies to tire.wav and audio/video containing it.
+
+All recorded masters are edited for fictional vehicles. No manufacturer
+affiliation or claim of exact engine reproduction. Engine variants use cuts,
+transposition, equalization, on-load/coast filtering and crossfaded loops.
+Body impacts use edited vehicle body/door recordings, not crash recordings.
+Wind and water noise beds are original offline sound design.
+Source/derivative filenames and SHA-256 values: manifest.json.
+All sources are local build inputs. The game makes no audio-generation/API calls.
